ation  but you must as I said validate it by  the 20th of December  everybody who validates his application  his or her application on the day of  closing will be invited to the first  stage of testing which is I said this  set of reasoning skills  we test your verbal numerical and  abstract reasoning skills  in your language one so one of the 24  languages of the EU you see here the  number of questions asked for each field  here the duration you get to solve these  questions and the scoring  there is no pass Mark for each of these  tests so you don't have to reach for  instance 10 out of 20 minimum or 5 out  of 10 minimum no you just have to score  well  and the people scoring overall so the  combined score  who scores the best after this uh after  these three tests will be invited to the  next stage so your overall score the  three points combined should be among  the X best to make it to stage number  two  I really suggest you train these kind of  tests  um you can do so on our website you see  the link on the bottom of this slide  here which leads you to the sample test  page on our website  where you find sample tests in each  language available for these different  skills here  please train this because by doing this  regularly by training this you get  better at solving these questions you  get to feel the difficulty of the  questions  and also there's this time factor  involved you must be able to solve these  questions quite fast and by doing this  many times you get better at this  so as I said the one's best scoring will  be invited to the second stage which is  the assessment center and here firstly  we test a set of General competencies  you see the seven General competencies  listed here and we assess these  competencies through two tests there is  a case study to be done the case study  will test four of these competencies and  then there's a situational  competency-based interview which will  assess three more competencies  the case study is written a written  exercise and the situation of  competency-based interview is an  interview where you are put in a work  related situation  and we basically want to see how you  react in that situation  you sit both these tests in your second  language so the one you indicated in  your application when you register for  this competition either English or  French  and you see the scoring 10 points to be  one per competency and here you need a  again a combined pass score of at least  35 out of 70. so in principle you could  fail for one or more competencies as  long as you make up for them in the  other competencies and as long as you  reach at least 35 out of 70 combined  apart from the general competencies we  also test of course field related  competencies in one of these fields of  the competition and we do this through  an interview again in your second  language and scoring is up to 100 points  and you need at least 50 out of 100 so  really an important part of the  selection of course  the ones with the overall best scores in  the assessment center so both the field  rated competency and the general  competencies  are the successful candidates  and you see again the numbers here that  we need per field so in total about 101  and these people are listed on this list  of successful candidates which will then  be recruited by the different EU  institutions and bodies  um I would really advise you again to  read the notice of competition very  carefully because it will give you very  detailed information about the job  description about the eligibility  criteria and about these different  stages of the tests uh if you would have  more questions for us related to this  competition you can always reach out to  us through the web form on our website  you can easily contact us please do also  follow us on the different social media  look for EU careers and you will find us  and you can follow us and we will update  you on different opportunities to come  and work for us  s